The `redeem()` function doesn't validate whether the market is listed or not before redeeming tokens, this could lead to a situation where users will be unable to redeem tokens from an unlisted market, causing transactions to be reverted. As a result, this would result in an increase in gas costs, which could lead to a loss of user funds. The [_checkRedeemAllowed()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-05-venus/blob/8be784ed9752b80e6f1b8b781e2e6251748d0d7e/contracts/Comptroller.sol#L1240-L1265) function is responsible for checking whether a user can redeem tokens from a market, but it doesn't address the issue of redeeming tokens from unlisted markets.
```solidity
    function _checkRedeemAllowed(
        address vToken,
        address redeemer,
        uint256 redeemTokens
    ) internal view {
        if (!markets[vToken].isListed) {
            revert MarketNotListed(address(vToken));
        }

        /* If the redeemer is not 'in' the market, then we can bypass the liquidity check */
        if (!markets[vToken].accountMembership[redeemer]) {
            return;
        }

        /* Otherwise, perform a hypothetical liquidity check to guard against shortfall */
        AccountLiquiditySnapshot memory snapshot = _getHypotheticalLiquiditySnapshot(
            redeemer,
            VToken(vToken),
            redeemTokens,
            0,
            _getCollateralFactor
        );
        if (snapshot.shortfall > 0) {
            revert InsufficientLiquidity();
        }
    }
```
